# 4. System Design and Implementation

This phase focused on replacing static content with real backend-driven data and improving communication between system components.

---

## 4.1 Backend Connection

The frontend mobile application was connected to backend services using API requests.

This allowed the application to:

* Send requests to backend APIs
* Retrieve landmark information
* Load nearby places dynamically
* Fetch categories and tourism-related data

---

## 4.2 Database Integration

The backend server was connected to a database to improve data storage and retrieval.

The database layer made it easier to:

* Store landmarks
* Save user-generated content
* Support dynamic filtering and search
* Prepare the system for future scalability

---

## 4.3 LLM Features

This week also included experimentation with LLM-based functionality.

These features can later support:

