# 6. Challenges and Problem Solving

Several technical challenges were encountered during this phase.

---

## Backend Connectivity Issues

Connecting the frontend to the backend server was difficult initially, especially on physical mobile devices.

`localhost` addresses did not work correctly, so local IP addresses had to be used instead.

---

## API Request Failures

Some API requests returned incorrect or empty responses because of:

* Route mismatches
* Formatting inconsistencies
* Incorrect request handling

---

## Database Migration Problems

Moving from hardcoded frontend data to database-driven content introduced inconsistencies in the data structure.

---

## LLM Response Formatting

LLM-generated responses were not always returned in a consistent structure.

Additional formatting and validation logic was required.

---

## Environment and Testing Issues

The backend environment occasionally behaved differently between:

* Local development
* Expo Go testing
* Physical device testing

